    "subtopic": "Rationalization of the Denominator",
    "difficulty": "MODERATE",
    "stem": "Rationalize the denominator \\(\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}}\\).",
    "solution": "The conjugate pair of \\(\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}\\) is \\(\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}\\).\n\\(\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}}=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}} \\times \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}{\\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right)^{2}-\\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)^{2}}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}{5-3}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)"
  },
