    "solution": "The conjugate pair of \\(3\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{5}\\) is \\(3\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{5}\\).\n\\(\\dfrac{8}{3\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{5}}=\\dfrac{8}{3\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{5}} \\times \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{5}}{3\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{5}}\\)\n\\(=\\dfrac{8\\left(3\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{5}\\right)}{\\left(3\\sqrt{2}\\right)^{2}-\\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right)^{2}}\\)\n\\(=\\dfrac{8 \\times 3\\sqrt{2}-8\\sqrt{5}}{9 \\times 2-5}=\\dfrac{24\\sqrt{2}-8\\sqrt{5}}{18-5}=\\dfrac{24\\sqrt{2}-8\\sqrt{5}}{13}\\)"
